WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.840
Ahsoka Tano was supposed to be Obi-Wan&nbsp;
Kenobi's Padawan but Yoda assigned her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.960
Anakin Skywaker instead. And it doesn't&nbsp;
get any less complicated from there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.720
Keep watching for all the ins and outs&nbsp;
of Ahsoka and Obi-Wan's relationship.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.000
One of the most interesting aspects of Obi-Wan&nbsp;
and Ahsoka's relationship is the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.080
he's basically her Jedi "grandfather." Jedi are&nbsp;
trained one-on-one, passing their teachings from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.880
master to student following specific generational&nbsp;
lines of Jedi that Ahsoka is proud to belong to.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.240
This Jedi legacy begins decades before&nbsp;
the films, when Jedi Grand Master Yoda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.760
decides to train a young boy named Dooku.&nbsp;
That boy grows up to train Qui-Gon Jinn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:49.600
the Jedi Master who discovers a small child named&nbsp;
Anakin Skywalker on the desert planet Tatooine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.880
But because Jinn is killed by Darth&nbsp;
Maul before he can train the boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:58.320
his former Padawan Obi-Wan Kenobi, takes&nbsp;
Anakin on as his apprentice in his stead.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.520
So, when Obi-Wan and Anakin fight Count Dooku&nbsp;
in "Attack of the Clones," they are, in a sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.960
fighting family. But, Jedi aren't meant to form&nbsp;
attachments or know their biological relatives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.920
As a result, the relationships between master&nbsp;
and apprentice are often the closest thing they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.800
have to parental bonds. So whenever Ahsoka&nbsp;
is instructed in the ways of the Force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.840
she is hearing the echoes of all&nbsp;
the Jedi who came before her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.120
whether she's hearing them directly&nbsp;
from Obi-Wan or through Anakin.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:25.680
What might have been

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.480
Strangely enough, Ahsoka was originally&nbsp;
meant to be Obi-Wan's second Padawan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.760
not Anakin's first. Obi-Wan puts in a request&nbsp;
for a new apprentice from the planet Christophsis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.480
shortly before the beginning of the 2008&nbsp;
animated film, "Star Wars: The Clone Wars."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.440
When Ahsoka arrives, Obi-Wan introduces&nbsp;
himself as her new master before Ahsoka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.280
corrects him and announces that she's&nbsp;
actually been assigned to Anakin.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.280
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.560
Though Obi-Wan seems surprised in the&nbsp;
moment, a later scene between Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.600
and Yoda seems to indicate that this has been&nbsp;
the duo's plan all along. That said, it's still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.760
interesting to wonder what their relationship&nbsp;
as master and apprentice would have been like.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.680
Obi-Wan has plenty of opportunities to train and&nbsp;
mentor the young Jedi throughout the Clone Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.160
as he, Anakin, and Ahsoka travel and&nbsp;
fight together more often than not.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.640
Obi-Wan Kenobi mentors Ahsoka&nbsp;
Tano in many different ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.880
but one of the most compelling is his&nbsp;
position as her commanding officer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.520
During the Clone Wars, the Jedi take on&nbsp;
official military ranks in the Grand Army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.080
of the Republic that directly correspond&nbsp;
to their ranks within the Jedi Order.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.560
Obi-Wan Kenobi becomes the High Jedi&nbsp;
General in charge of the 7th Sky Corps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:47.200
alongside Clone Marshal Commander CC-2224, aka&nbsp;
"Cody." Anakin's clone legion, the famous 501st,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.880
is one of many legions under the 7th Sky Corps,&nbsp;
and, as such, is under the overarching command&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.520
of Obi-Wan. Though the two are no longer&nbsp;
master and apprentice, Obi-Wan is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.320
Anakin's commanding officer, which makes&nbsp;
Obi-Wan responsible for Ahsoka as well.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.720
"Star Wars: The Clone Wars" features a large&nbsp;
cast of characters. However, Anakin Skywalker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:14.480
Obi-Wan Kenobi, and Ahsoka Tano become the&nbsp;
closest thing the series has to main characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.520
The three work closely&nbsp;
together throughout the war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.320
and any story that features one of them&nbsp;
almost always features the other two as well.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.200
"The Clone Wars" explores the galaxy's&nbsp;
journey between the events of "Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:33.200
Episode II — Attack of the Clones" and those&nbsp;
of "Star Wars: Episode III — Revenge of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.080
Sith." Ahsoka is the most important&nbsp;
new character the show introduces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.440
so it's only natural that she join Anakin&nbsp;
and Obi-Wan as the show's lead characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.880
The movie that kicks off their story begins with&nbsp;
their first meeting. And then, the last story of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:55.680
the series' ending season begins with their final&nbsp;
encounter. Then, Order 66 changes everything.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.680
Though this might seem like an unorthodox way&nbsp;
to put it, Obi-Wan basically helps Anakin raise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:07.440
Ahsoka. Over the course of the war, the three of&nbsp;
them work together on many different missions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.760
This is a time of tremendous growth for Ahsoka,&nbsp;
which Obi-Wan is almost entirely present for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.840
And so, Obi-Wan helps guide Anakin as he trains&nbsp;
Ahsoka and learns how to be a teacher. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:25.040
Ahsoka often looks to Obi-Wan for guidance as&nbsp;
she learns to navigate the universe at large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.600
and her master's unique tendencies.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:34.240
The two Jedi teach Ahsoka how to be the best&nbsp;
person, Jedi, leader, and soldier that she can be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.240
She keeps those teachings with her&nbsp;
as she rebels against the Empire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.320
long after the Clone Wars come&nbsp;
to an end. Ahsoka comes to regard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.840
Obi-Wan and Anakin as one does their parents. For&nbsp;
all intents and purposes, they are her parents.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:53.120
While Obi-Wan is patient, humble, and&nbsp;
forward-thinking, Anakin is impulsive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.080
overconfident, and eager to rush into danger.&nbsp;
The fact that they come to balance each other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.720
out is a large part of what makes them&nbsp;
such an incredible team. It's no surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:08.320
then, that Ahsoka, a student of both Jedi,&nbsp;
comes to embody the balance between them.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.920
When she first begins as Anakin's Padawan, Ahsoka&nbsp;
is arrogant and quick to jump the gun. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:20.480
she's intelligent and competent, she's also often&nbsp;
right, which fuels her recklessness. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:26.720
a series of mistakes teaches her humility. In&nbsp;
this sense, she's quite similar to her master.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.360
By the time the Clone Wars finally end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:35.040
she develops a patience strongly reminiscent of&nbsp;
Obi-Wan's. This results in a best-of-both-worlds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:40.400
balance. Like Anakin, Ahsoka never&nbsp;
hesitates to leap to someone's aid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:45.760
but like Obi-Wan, she knows the value of slowing&nbsp;
down to plan before deciding her next move.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.840
"You have one day to decide."

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:01.760
In Season 4's "Kidnapped," Anakin, Ahsoka, and&nbsp;
Obi-Wan investigate the disappearance of a colony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:07.440
of Ahsoka's species, called Togrutas. When they&nbsp;
arrive, the trio discover that the entire colony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:14.240
has been taken by Zygerrian slavers. Anakin is&nbsp;
furious, and though it's obvious to Ahsoka why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:20.880
her master finds slavery abhorrent, she doesn't&nbsp;
understand his personal stake in the crime.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:26.080
It's at this point the audience realizes Anakin&nbsp;
has told Ahsoka nothing of his own history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.600
So, when Ahsoka asks Obi-Wan&nbsp;
about it after Anakin leaves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:34.640
he tells her about her master's childhood&nbsp;
in slavery. It's a fascinating scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:40.640
and it illustrates the trio's relationship well:&nbsp;
When Anakin shuts her out, Ahsoka goes to Obi-Wan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:45.840
who tells her what she needs to know while&nbsp;
still respecting Anakin's desire for privacy.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:52.000
In the final arc of "The Clone Wars" Season&nbsp;
5, Ahsoka is put through one of the worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:57.920
experiences of her life. She is framed for&nbsp;
bombing the Jedi Temple, even though she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:03.440
in another part of the galaxy when it happened.&nbsp;
Many Jedi do not believe her, and a warrant is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:08.240
placed for her arrest, forcing her to flee&nbsp;
and attempt to clear her name on her own.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:14.240
When the Jedi finally catch her, they decide&nbsp;
to put her on trial. But, at Supreme Chancellor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.280
Palpatine's request, the Jedi agree to have&nbsp;
Ahsoka face court as a military officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:24.800
and not a Jedi. So, Ahsoka finds herself&nbsp;
before a Republic military tribunal.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:31.920
In order for Ahsoka to be judged by the Republic,&nbsp;
she must first be expelled from the Jedi Order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:38.000
Though Obi-Wan initially tries to stand up for&nbsp;
Ahsoka, he ultimately relents and sides with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:44.480
rest of the Council. And so, by a near-unanimous&nbsp;
vote, the Jedi Council casts Ahsoka out.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:50.000
When Anakin finally clears her name,&nbsp;
Ahsoka is invited to rejoin the order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.400
But the sting of this betrayal&nbsp;
still lingers, and she refuses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.400 --> 00:08:00.320
Ahsoka loves and trusts Obi-Wan, but when she&nbsp;
needs him most, he does not have her back.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.680
Anakin and Obi-Wan don't discuss Ahsoka's&nbsp;
departure from the Jedi Order until Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.800
7. However, a canceled story arc called&nbsp;
"Crystal Crisis on Utapau" was originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:15.120
set to address her absence. The&nbsp;
arc is still considered canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:20.800
and story reels of the unfinished episodes&nbsp;
were eventually released on StarWars-dot-com.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.920
In the arc's second episode, "In Search of the&nbsp;
Crystal," Anakin mentions Ahsoka for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:31.040
time since the incident, prompting a discussion&nbsp;
with Obi-Wan as they set up camp for the night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:36.320
Anakin tells his master how much he misses his&nbsp;
former Padawan, and is obviously angry that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:41.680
left the Order. But when Obi-Wan emphasizes that&nbsp;
it was her decision to leave, Anakin responds,

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.880
"Well, what choice did we give her?"

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.680
Anakin blames the Council for refusing&nbsp;
to stand by Ahsoka in her time of need,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:56.720
but Obi-Wan disagrees. He blames Ahsoka, claiming&nbsp;
her emotions affected her decision. Since that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:02.560
against the Jedi code, it is thus her failure&nbsp;
to act like a Jedi that caused her to leave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.240
He effectively paints her leaving&nbsp;
as some sort of childish tantrum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.520
completely disregarding the&nbsp;
legitimacy of her position.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:16.320
Obi-Wan Kenobi seems like the definitive Jedi.&nbsp;
He's humble, compassionate, and self-controlled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:22.880
But Ahsoka comes to believe that Obi-Wan embodies&nbsp;
the Jedi Order's flaws. During the war, the Jedi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:28.960
become dominated by politics, and transform&nbsp;
from peacekeeping monks into generals of one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:34.800
of the galaxy's largest armies. This ultimately&nbsp;
blinds them to the needs of the common man.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:40.640
When the Jedi Council exiles Ahsoka, they do&nbsp;
so because they don't want the Senate to think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:46.640
they've lost their impartiality. Though there is&nbsp;
wisdom in this, they fail to take any additional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:53.680
action to protect Ahsoka, or discover what&nbsp;
truly happened. Instead, they abandon her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:58.240
which forces her to rethink everything&nbsp;
she once believed about the Order.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:04.240
This comes to a head in Season 7's "Old Friends&nbsp;
Not Forgotten." When Ahsoka asks her old masters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:10.080
to help against Maul on Mandalore, they abandon&nbsp;
her again to rush to the Battle of Coruscant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:14.560
When she challenges their decision,&nbsp;
Obi-Wan says that Coruscant's people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:19.680
need them. But, Ahsoka rightly states that&nbsp;
they're going only for the Chancellor.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.840
Once again, they're playing&nbsp;
politics instead of helping people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:29.920
It's the Jedis' duty to serve everybody, not&nbsp;
just one man. In calling her old masters out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.560
Ahsoka illustrates something she&nbsp;
says in Season 3's "The Academy,"

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.120
"It's every citizen's duty&nbsp;
to challenge their leaders."

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:44.640
In E. K. Johnston's novel, "Star Wars: Ahsoka,"&nbsp;
readers join Ahsoka Tano a year after Order 66.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:49.920
At this point, the former Jedi is still alone&nbsp;
and on the run from the Empire. She hasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:55.360
yet joined any rebellions or even started to&nbsp;
process all that she has lost. But when a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:00.320
acquaintance asks her about her past, she&nbsp;
claims to be an orphan who was "adopted."

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.760
Obviously, she's hiding the truth of her past&nbsp;
as a Jedi who was raised in the Jedi Temple.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:11.520
But throughout the exchange, she refers to Anakin&nbsp;
and Obi-Wan as her adoptive parents, and smiles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:17.040
fondly as she remembers how they constantly&nbsp;
bickered, quote, "like an old married couple."

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:22.640
Despite how strained and broken their relationship&nbsp;
has become by this point, Ahsoka still chooses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:29.280
to remember Obi-Wan with warmth and love. She&nbsp;
accepts how important he is to her, flaws and all.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:36.480
Following the bloody rampage of Order 66&nbsp;
Ahsoka mourns Obi-Wan, which is made all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:42.640
the more tragic by the fact that Obi-Wan isn't&nbsp;
actually dead. Unbeknownst to either character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:48.000
they both survive the Great Jedi Purge and&nbsp;
go on to oppose the Empire in their own ways.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:54.160
Only Bail Organa and Yoda know that Obi-Wan&nbsp;
goes into hiding on the planet Tatooine to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:59.200
protect his former pupil's son, Luke.&nbsp;
Ahsoka eventually joins forces with Bail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:05.200
Organa and works closely with him in forming the&nbsp;
Rebellion. But, he never reveals Obi-Wan's fate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:11.840
The existence of Anakin's child is simply too&nbsp;
important to risk telling anybody, even Ahsoka.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:17.920
Likewise, Obi-Wan is purposefully out of contact&nbsp;
with the rest of the galaxy, which means nobody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:22.800
can tell him about Ahsoka. When he leaves&nbsp;
Tatooine with Luke aboard the Millennium Falcon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:27.680
everybody believes Ahsoka is dead. By&nbsp;
the time anyone knows that wasn't true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:33.440
Obi-Wan has been killed by his own apprentice,&nbsp;
by then known as the fearsome Darth Vader.&nbsp;

